----------------------------------------------------------------------
3. COMPARISON AND INTERPRETATION:
----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Coordinate System      | Rank  | Null Dim | Invariant | Status
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Log-space (f=log)      | 15/18 |    3     |    3      | ✓ PASS
  Original-space         | 15/18 |    3     |    0      | ✗ FAIL

  Key Insights:
    ✓ Rank is coordinate-independent: 15 == 15
      → This is a topological property of the auxiliary map
    ✗ Null space invariance IS coordinate-dependent!
      → Log-space: 3/3 null vectors invariant
      → Original-space: 0/3 null vectors invariant
    → Log-transform gives minimal image (invariant null space)
    → Original coordinates give only rank-deficient manifold
    → Invariance test identifies 'right' coordinate system for monomials

  Why This Matters:
    • Not all rank-deficient manifolds are minimal images
    • SVD alone cannot distinguish them
    • Invariance test (Algorithm 1) is essential, not optional
    • For monomial reparameterizations, log-transform is principled choice

